  "id": "WI-0088",
  "title": "Add real-browser Management Console regression coverage",
  "state": "done",
  "owner_position": "engineering_manager",
  "assigned_agent_id": "agent-mog",
  "created_at": "2026-09-01T15:25:03.827Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-09-01T15:42:09.595Z",
  "scope": [
    "Add a pinned, license-reviewed Playwright Core development integration that launches installed Google Chrome without downloading a browser, starts the repository-local Control Plane on loopback, and verifies the human-facing Management Console in a real browser.",
    "Cover mobile, tablet, desktop, and ultrawide layouts; navigation, live rendering, console errors, keyboard tab behavior, reduced motion, horizontal overflow, clipping, and overlap must fail with actionable diagnostics and a screenshot.",
    "Run the browser gate only in the Node.js 24 full hosted lane so documentation and evidence-only changes keep their measured low-cost path and the Node.js 22 compatibility lane is not duplicated."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "A real browser opens the live repository-backed Management Console at 390x844, 768x1024, 1440x1000, and 3440x1440; every primary view renders, navigation works, and no viewport has document-level horizontal overflow, clipped primary text, or overlapping high-level layout regions.",
    "Browser console errors, unhandled page errors, inaccessible primary navigation, incorrect mobile sidebar behavior, broken organization tabs, and reduced-motion regressions fail the gate; a failure screenshot is written below output/playwright/.",
    "Playwright Core is pinned exactly, its Apache-2.0 license and non-runtime purpose are recorded, no browser binary is vendored or downloaded by the repository, and the integration has contract tests.",
    "GitHub CI runs the browser gate only for the Node.js 24 full scope and includes it in the aggregated blocking result without adding a separate billed job."
  ],
